        "reviewed": true,
        "context_checked": true,
        "method": "Published author proof/core and local context fidelity screening",
        "note": "Select Theorem3.8 for d>=3 and finite positive noninteger m, with smooth Riemannian g, positive smooth f and real curvature parameter mu. Thus d+m is noninteger, and the claim is existence of a straight normal dilation-homogeneous Lorentzian metric/function near the metric cone whose weighted Ricci tensor and F vanish to infinite order in rho, unique modulo O(rho^infinity); it is not an exact convergent Ricci-flat PDE solution. The full local author normal-form computation, correction matrices4.3/4.5, determinant and Borel construction in4.5(i), and the remaining-component Bianchi proof of3.8 are included. Normal/straight definitions, weighted contracted Bianchi identity2.2 and density conventions are preserved. Existing unweighted straight-metric characterizations are background; the new coupled metric/function correction and weighted mixed-component argument are explicitly written. Integer warped-product specializations, resonant even/odd cases, Poincare and GJMS consequences are not separately counted."
      },
